.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS7_SIGN 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS7_sign_ex ,
.Nm PKCS7_sign
.Nd create a PKCS#7 signedData structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs7.h
.Ft PKCS7 *
.Fo PKCS7_sign_ex
.Fa "X509 *signcert"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *certs"
.Fa "BIO *data"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft PKCS7 *
.Fo PKCS7_sign
.Fa "X509 *signcert"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *certs"
.Fa "BIO *data"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PKCS7_sign_ex
creates and returns a PKCS#7 signedData structure.
.Fa signcert
is the certificate to sign with,
.Fa pkey
is the corresponding private key.
.Fa certs
is an optional set of extra certificates to include in the PKCS#7
structure (for example any intermediate CAs in the chain).
The library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq
are used when retrieving algorithms from providers.
.Pp
The data to be signed is read from BIO
.Fa data .
.Pp
.Fa flags
is an optional set of flags.
.Pp
Any of the following flags (ored together) can be passed in the
.Fa flags
parameter.
.Pp
Many S/MIME clients expect the signed content to include valid MIME
headers.
If the
.Sy PKCS7_TEXT
flag is set MIME headers for type
.Qo Li text/plain Qc
are prepended to the data.
.Pp
If
.Sy PKCS7_NOCERTS
is set the signer's certificate and the extra
.Fa certs
will not be included in the PKCS7 structure.
The signer's certificate must still be supplied in the
.Fa signcert
parameter though.
This can reduce the size of the signatures if the signer's certificates
can be obtained by other means: for example a previously signed message.
.Pp
The data being signed is included in the PKCS7 structure, unless
.Sy PKCS7_DETACHED
is set in which case it is omitted.
This is used for PKCS7 detached signatures which are used in S/MIME
plaintext signed messages for example.
.Pp
Normally the supplied content is translated into MIME canonical format
(as required by the S/MIME specifications) if
.Sy PKCS7_BINARY
is set no translation occurs.
This option should be used if the supplied data is in binary format
otherwise the translation will corrupt it.
.Pp
The signedData structure includes several PKCS#7 authenticatedAttributes
including the signing time, the PKCS#7 content type and the supported
list of ciphers in an SMIMECapabilities attribute.
If
.Sy PKCS7_NOATTR
is set then no authenticatedAttributes will be used.
If
.Sy PKCS7_NOSMIMECAP
is set then just the SMIMECapabilities are omitted.
.Pp
If present the SMIMECapabilities attribute indicates support for the
following algorithms: triple DES, 128 bit RC2, 64 bit RC2, DES and 40
bit RC2. If any of these algorithms is disabled then it will not be
included.
.Pp
If the flags
.Sy PKCS7_STREAM
is set then the returned
.Vt PKCS7
structure is just initialized ready to perform the signing operation.
The signing is however
.Sy not
performed and the data to be signed is not read from the
.Fa data
parameter.
Signing is deferred until after the data has been written.
In this way data can be signed in a single pass.
.Pp
If the
.Sy PKCS7_PARTIAL
flag is set a partial
.Vt PKCS7
structure is output to which additional signers and capabilities can be
added before finalization.
.Pp
If the flag
.Sy PKCS7_STREAM
is set the returned
.Vt PKCS7
structure is
.Sy not
complete and outputting its contents via a function that does not
properly finalize the
.Vt PKCS7
structure will give unpredictable results.
.Pp
Several functions including
.Xr SMIME_write_PKCS7 3 ,
.Xr i2d_PKCS7_bio_stream 3 ,
.Xr PEM_write_bio_PKCS7_stream 3
finalize the structure.
Alternatively finalization can be performed by obtaining the streaming
ASN1
.Vt BIO
directly using
.Xr BIO_new_PKCS7 3 .
.Pp
If a signer is specified it will use the default digest for the signing
algorithm.
This is
.Sy SHA256
for both RSA and DSA keys.
.Pp
The
.Fa certs ,
.Fa signcert
and
.Fa pkey
parameters can all be NULL if the
.Sy PKCS7_PARTIAL
flag is set.
One or more signers can be added using the function
.Xr PKCS7_sign_add_signer 3 .
.Xr PKCS7_final 3
must also be called to finalize the structure if streaming is not
enabled.
Alternative signing digests can also be specified using this method.
.Pp
If
.Fa signcert
and
.Fa pkey
are NULL then a certificates only PKCS#7 structure is output.
.Pp
In versions of OpenSSL before 1.0.0 the
.Fa signcert
and
.Fa pkey
parameters must not be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS7_sign
is like
.Fn PKCS7_sign_ex
except that it uses default values of NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq .
This is retained for API backward compatibility.
.Sh BUGS
Some advanced attributes such as counter signatures are not supported.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn PKCS7_sign_ex
and
.Fn PKCS7_sign
return either a valid PKCS7 structure or NULL if an error occurred.
The error can be obtained from ERR_get_error(3).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr PKCS7_verify 3
.Sh HISTORY
The function
.Fn PKCS7_sign_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Sy PKCS7_PARTIAL
flag, and the ability for
.Fa certs ,
.Fa signcert ,
and
.Fa pkey
parameters to be NULL were added in OpenSSL 1.0.0.
.Pp
The
.Sy PKCS7_STREAM
flag was added in OpenSSL 1.0.0.
